WEBVTT

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.010
Enjoy.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.610
Thank you.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.170
I made it a little strong, because you seem tired.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.650
Is that all right?

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.660
You read me like a book. It's delicious.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.750
I'm glad I didn't bring an umbrella.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.280
It gives me an excuse to stay a while.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.810
That's true.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:01.900
This mysterious restaurant is on a road just a little ways from the center of Rome.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:08.030
casetta dell'orso

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:08.710
Huh?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.500
Is there a special guest coming tonight?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.960
A certain someone from the past is coming with the owner and his wife tonight.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.800
Oh?

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.050
Say, what is "Teo's Specially-made Dolce Piatto" exactly?

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:31.240
Well, he's not much for Teo's dolce, actually.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.740
Buonasera.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.680
Buonasera.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.750
Well, it's been a while, Claudio.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.860
We've been expecting you, Marzio.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.280
The owner and his wife haven't arrived yet.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.750
You all look well.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.710
I hear about the restaurant here and there.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.550
Have you lost weight?

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.950
That's because Gigi and I used to eat a ton, back then.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.950
Speaking of Gigi...

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.730
He hasn't changed a bit.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.340
Eating as always.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.700
Who is that?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.670
Are you sure, Gigi?

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.420
Huh? Isn't that one of the really expensive bottles?

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.820
Who is that man?

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.250
Ah!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.370
Nicoletta, come out here.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:43.040
But I promised not to leave the kitchen...

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.770
Today's a special occasion.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.770
Come on, introduce yourself to your predecessor.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.660
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Nicoletta.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.570
I'm Marzio.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.670
Looks like you've hired another cute, young lady again, huh?

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.370
He used to help in the kitchen.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.670
Besides for Gigi, he's been in the business for longer than anyone.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.100
Dell'orso has quite the past.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.820
You overworked yourself.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.590
Should I call your folks?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.280
It's OK.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.670
After you're discharged tomorrow, want to stop for a drink on the way home?

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.700
You know, at the bar he works at.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.660
Yeah... OK. Let's do that.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.370
I'm feeling better already.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.870
Buonasera.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.630
Where's that man? That older barista.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:13.390
Oh, my brother-in-law? He hasn't worked here since last week.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.420
What?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.320
What? He quit?!

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.090
Really?

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:27.130
Ah, I get it. That's why you came along to get me, Gigi.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.810
And wearing a suit on your day off...

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:36.590
I used to spend my days, waiting for work to get out, so I could go there.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.910
There are plenty of gentlemen in town,

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:44.730
but a place where you can have a drink and truly be at ease is rare indeed.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.900
Would that be strange?

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.340
There's still that cameriere left...

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.090
What about the barista from that bar?

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.800
Yeah, I had the same thought, so I got his name and phone number.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.040
Luciano De Luca...

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.000
I'm afraid I'll have to pass.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.370
I just grew tired of working as a barista, so I quit.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.660
I don't think I can go back to working the late shift...

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:33.880
Quit? Didn't you just use your sick days to spend some time with your grandson?

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.810
But still, it's a great opportunity.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:42.120
You're more suited to being a cameriere than a barista, I bet.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.370
You stay out of this.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.880
There are plenty of young men who can be camerieres.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.610
Why would you want someone like me?

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.460
To be honest, it's for my wife.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.470
For your wife?

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:05.680
She's got what you'd call peculiar tastes...

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.980
We've been planning on opening the ristorante for months,

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:15.170
but she collapsed the other day, from overworking.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:17.460
So, I'd like to do something for her.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.770
I'll introduce you to someone else.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.510
Just accept that and go, please.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.330
He's a gentleman.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:33.410
How can I put it... A real man.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:41.520
I've been working at a ristorante outside of Rome.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.380
I've been there about twenty years.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.430
Twenty years, you say?

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:50.610
The owner there has been very generous to me,

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.530
but he passed away recently...

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.520
The new owner doesn't take as kindly to me...

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:00.940
I'm sure he knows what I'm referring to.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.830
I heard you used to work together...

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.230
He's a brilliant man.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.100
He's incredibly sophisticated...

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.120
But, he had to quit when his wife got sick.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:42.600
So, I'm sure he'll sympathize with the emotions you have towards your wife.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:46.850
I'd love for him to work for me.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.620
Say no more. I'll convince him for you.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.720
Thank you. But, what about yourself?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:00.920
I'd like to mull it over a bit more.

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.210
I've worked at the same place for a long time.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.630
Of course.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.800
We convinced each other.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:15.720
Some Orsini wine was involved.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.340
Thank you both.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.730
However, there's that sign out back...

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:27.900
Seeking bespectacled men, fifty or older...

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.400
Just saw this, guys. What do you say?

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.450
Oh.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.210
Forgive my attire. I was out for a jog.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:44.880
Let me get my spectacles.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.780
I've got no experience as a cameriere,

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.870
but I've worked plenty of different jobs.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.930
As a concierge in a hotel, etc.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.920
I'd love to try and work as a cameriere.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.940
He looks like a nice guy.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.400
Indeed.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:09.460
Allow me to introduce you all once again. This is an old associate of mine, Marzio.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:15.210
He used to help out in the kitchen sometimes, when I ran the restaurant next to the winery.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.880
These are the chefs, Vanna and Dario.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.710
They're both masters in the kitchen.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.860
Claudio, a cameriere.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.750
Also, Luciano and Vito.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.200
These are the gentlemen who will manage the floor.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.410
They're all old men.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.720
Seriously.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:34.760
And this is Gigi, our sommelier.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.210
This is the wine list.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:39.880
This is the food menu.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:44.670
I'll switch it up seasonly, but we'll start with this.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:59.100
Oh, right. They all wear spectacles.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.870
It's no big deal. Don't worry about it.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.490
I hope this puts a smile on her face.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:43.530
The owner and his wife sure are late, huh?

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.960
He told me to get here before it opens.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:50.090
I'm hungry, Grandpa.

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:51.940
Just a little longer, dear.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:59.990
I'm sure <i>she's</i> still at work... My goodness.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.120
Buonasera.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:03.470
Buonasera.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.100
Buonasera.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.850
I'll take your coats.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.510
Right this way.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:19.000
How about you bring out a little of the food they make for the staff?

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.500
Not a problem.

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:24.850
We'll move you to your table when the owner and his wife show up.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:29.510
Nicoletta, keep them company in their place.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:30.910
Huh? But...

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.070
I'll let the kitchen staff know.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.340
Th-Thank you.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:40.320
The dinner service won't hit its peak for a bit.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.840
Also, part of your job is to learn the restaurant's history.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:45.980
Right.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.730
Eat up.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.690
Twenty years already...

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.570
That's so cool.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:00.460
I've got to work my hardest, too.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:06.940
There's so much about Claudio I don't know.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.930
Being invited in before it even opens... I'm so excited!

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:20.060
I wonder what the ristorante will be like.

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:24.570
I made special reservations. Let's just take our time and enjoy ourselves.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.250
Bear Street...

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:49.370
This is it, huh?

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:53.370
Ristorante casetta dell'orso.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:05.440
Madam, will it be to your liking?

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.790
I won't pull any punches.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:15.700
Buonasera.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:22.760
B-Buonasera.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:25.180
Allow me to take your shawl.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.620
Grazie.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.050
Right this way.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:45.970
It's beautiful.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.690
Want to relax a little more?

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.230
Yes.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.030
Order anything on the menu.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:10.930
I wonder what I should get...

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.010
Here is the menu.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:21.850
We've prepared a special menu to pair with the Orsini wine that you like so much.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.020
I'm delighted.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.200
What does that entail?

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.230
Allow me.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:36.080
Yes, it includes seasonal mushrooms.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.010
We'll be serving porcini mushrooms tonight.

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:43.290
H-He's a complete gentleman...

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.450
And he's wearing spectacles!

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.650
Eggplant is in season now.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.840
We'll be including it in tonight's antipasto.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:02.790
I cannot fathom another restaurant this wonderful.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.610
Both the food and wine are delectable,

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.630
and so is the scenery!

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.390
You know, I'd like to meet the chef, too.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.220
Sure she won't mind the fact that I'm not a gentleman?

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.990
It's fine, fine.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:25.290
I'm just the sous chef.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.030
Dario?

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.980
Everyone who works here is older!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.260
That's wonderful!

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:39.700
I'll revisit this situation when I'm an older man.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.420
So, do you like it?

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:53.420
I...

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.940
More than anything else...

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:03.450
The fact that you thought of me this much makes me so happy, Lorenzo!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.500
It was a splendid evening.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:29.950
Wow, I had no idea.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:38.170
Oh, I see you told her about that night.

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.320
When I saw the two of them that night,

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:48.530
I just knew.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.110
Huh?

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:53.610
I knew I'd love this place for a long time to come.

00:18:54.470 --> 00:19:00.480
This restaurant's origins go back to the owner's deep love for his wife.

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:04.120
Yeah.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:07.830
Be that as it may, they sure are late.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.770
Buonasera.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:12.710
I got here as quickly as I could.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.140
It appears he's arrived.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.650
I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.270
Olga wanted to give this to you.

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:28.580
She couldn't break away from work. I apologize.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:32.580
I'll catch her next time, then.

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.220
Come on, let me buy you a drink, Lorenzo.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:36.870
Sure. That's a fantastic idea.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:38.990
OK, how about...

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:40.500
She is such a bad person.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:43.170
You planning on taking the whole night off?

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.560
I was just on my way back to the kitchen!

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.830
Get to work.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:53.590
I will! I'll work for twenty years!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.870
You worked late tonight.

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:19.080
Sorry, it was so hectic today.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.560
Let's invite Marzio out the next chance we get.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.090
We can have him join us at the end of the day, like this.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:32.600
Seeing you smile cleanses my soul.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:43.910
Grazie.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:46.900
Prego.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:21:15.950
The Flavor of Orsini

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:12.240
We're not involved in their feud,

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:15.240
so let's stay on good terms, Gigi.

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.560
Let's stay on good terms and watch the next episode together...
